   "kind": "antenna",
   "dead_dir": [
    0.0,
    -1.0
   ],
   "note": "PCB trace antenna for 433.92 MHz ASK / FSK modules, key fobs, remote sockets (EU ISM). A STARTING POINT: 116 mm of 1 mm copper (quarter wave 105 mm from the FR4 rule of thumb, effective permittivity 2.7, plus 10 % to trim). Pin 1 = feed (the radio's RF pin, through any matching parts), pins 2 and 3 = ground: put ground copper or the ground fill beside them, never above the feed. Silk ticks every 2 mm from the tip; the longer tick is the formula length. Measure with a NanoVNA and scratch the copper back from the tip until it is best at your frequency; if it resonates too high add copper instead. The box is a keep-out: no copper, fill or back-side plane inside it. Untested on a real board.",
